THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

The license above covers the tseries Dart code, the C shim in `native/` and
tseries' own C replacements in `third_party/ctsa_replacements/`. The native
core is the vendored ctsa library in `third_party/ctsa/`
(https://github.com/rafat/ctsa), compiled into the `ctsa` code asset. That tree
is mixed-license; its components and their notices follow. Per-file and
per-function licensing is marked with SPDX-License-Identifier comments in the
vendored sources.

LGPL: none. The units upstream marks LGPL-3.0-or-later (`src/brent.c`,
`src/brent.h`, `src/erfunc.c` and two sections of `src/dist.c`) have been
removed from this tree and replaced by independent BSD-3-Clause
implementations; see `third_party/ctsa/PROVENANCE.md`.

Also replaced or removed for licensing reasons (same file): ACM Algorithm 419
(`src/polyroot.c`, ACM non-commercial licence) and `ppsum()` of `src/talg.c`
(from the GPL R package tseries) are replaced by BSD-3-Clause code in
`third_party/ctsa_replacements/`; unreachable Numerical Recipes routines
(`src/matrix.c`), Applied Statistics algorithm AS 197 (`src/emle.c`,
`src/talg.c`) and C versions of R's ARIMA parameter transforms (`src/talg.c`)
are deleted. The auto-ARIMA code — a C version of GPL-licensed R code (the
order search in `src/ctsa.c`, `src/autoutils.c` and `src/seastest.c` from the
R package forecast, `src/unitroot.c` from R packages tseries/urca, `src/stl.c`
from R's modified netlib STL, and `supsmu` in `src/talg.c`) — is deleted in
0.8.0; order selection (`autoArima`) is tseries' own Dart code. The
unaudited `sarimax_wrapper()` group of `src/ctsa.c` (never called by tseries)
and `src/boxcox.c`, its last user, are deleted as well.

OPEN LICENSING QUESTIONS (engineering notes, not legal advice) — see
`third_party/ctsa/PROVENANCE.md`, "License audit" and "Open licensing
questions", for detail:
  * `src/emle.c` contains C translations of Applied Statistics algorithms
    AS 154, AS 182 and AS 75 (exact ARIMA likelihood, forecasting, and the
    least-squares helper they use); `src/neldermead.c` contains AS 47 (linked,
    not used by tseries). StatLib states that the Royal Statistical Society
    holds the copyright and permits distribution "provided that no fee is
    charged". This code runs on every fit and forecast.
  Its status has not been resolved. (`src/initest.c`, a "C translation of
  Cedrick Collomb's C++ Implementation" of Burg's method for which no licence
  was found, was unreachable and has been deleted.)

